  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Blender Exports**\n\nI\'ve made a key discovery: both `concrete-fence-1a.glb` and `barricade-1a.glb` utilized a `.REF` node during Blender export, indicating a canonical reference. Now, I\'m examining what the `ConcreteFence_1A.REF` file actually contains, especially node 6, `ConcreteFence_1A`.\n\n\n**Revisiting User Instructions**\n\nI\'ve circled back to the user\'s prompt and realized I missed crucial instructions! I\'m now meticulously re-evaluating the request to replace the barricade walls around the \'Blue Base\' and \'Red Base\' with \'concrete-fence-1a.glb\'. I had overlooked the directive to arrange the fences edge-to-edge, maintaining the original sub-mesh structure, which is a key part of the \'concrete-fence-1a.glb\' model. This impacts how I should address the `.REF` and geometry information.\n\n\n**Refining UI Cleanup Process**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in auditing and overhauling the UI text and elements, aiming for extreme clarity, minimalism, and child-friendliness as specified. I\'m focusing on the literal application of all rules, especially around eliminating improvisation, excessive word count, and unauthorized icons/emojis. The primary focus is cleaning up the book cards, the top bookshelf, side items, and footer/banner. The constraint of adhering to literal compliance guides the current implementation of changes.\n\n\n"
