  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Testing the Loading Process**\n\nI\'m now writing a script to load `concrete-fence-1a.glb` using Three.js\'s `GLTFLoader` and `DRACOLoader`. I\'m using either TSX or Node, since the project has both, to see the behavior firsthand. This approach allows me to examine the loading sequence and identify any potential issues in the actual implementation.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_140622"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"npx tsx -e \\\"\\nimport * as THREE from \'three\';\\nimport { GLTFLoader } from \'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js\';\\nimport { DRACOLoader } from \'three/addons/loaders/DRACOLoader.js\';\\nimport fs from \'fs\';\\n\\nconst dracoLoader = new DRACOLoader();\\n// draco decoder path\\ndracoLoader.setDecoderPath(\'public/draco/\');\\n\\nconst loader = new GLTFLoader();\\nloader.setDRACOLoader(dracoLoader);\\n\\nconst data = fs.readFileSync(\'public/extracted_lyo_assets/models/concrete-fence-1a.glb\');\\nconst ab = data.buffer.slice(data.byteOffset, data.byteOffset + data.byteLength);\\n\\nloader.parse(ab, \'\', (gltf) => {\\n  console.log(\'GLTF loaded successfully!\');\\n  console.log(\'Scene children count:\', gltf.scene.children.length);\\n  gltf.scene.traverse((obj) => {\\n    console.log(\'Node:\', obj.name, obj.type, \'pos:\', obj.position.toArray(), \'rot:\', obj.rotation.toArray(), \'scale:\', obj.scale.toArray());\\n    if (obj.isMesh) {\\n      obj.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\\n      console.log(\'  Mesh bbox:\', obj.geometry.boundingBox.min.toArray(), \'to\', obj.geometry.boundingBox.max.toArray());\\n    }\\n  });\\n}, (err) => {\\n  console.error(\'Error loading:\', err);\\n});\\n\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":5000,\"toolAction\":\"Inspecting model hierarchy\",\"toolSummary\":\"Run tsx script to inspect GLTF with Three.js\"}"
