    thinking: "**Analyzing the Scene Graph**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the scene graph of `concrete-fence-1a.glb`. It appears to be composed of several nodes: `ConcreteFence_1A.001`, `ConcreteFence_1A.002`, `ConcreteFence_1A.003`, `ConcreteFence_1A.004`, and `ConcreteFence_1A.005`. This breakdown suggests a modular design, or perhaps different parts of a larger fence structure. I\'m noting each node name carefully as I analyze the whole.\n\n\n**Examining the Code Flow**\n\nI\'ve traced the execution path related to `concrete-fence-1a.glb` in `spawnRealLyoPropFromGlb`. The code isolates `ConcreteFence_1A.REF`, which then traverses its children. Specifically, it identifies and processes a Mesh named `Plane.20009` representing a single fence section and the `cuboid_fixed.009` which is ignored due to being a collider.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user\'s intent, particularly the \"barricade walls\" and the \"edge-to-edge\" arrangement around the \'Blue Base\' and \'Red Base\'. I\'m recognizing that the `concrete-fence-1a.glb` model likely represents a single concrete fence unit, not the complete barricade itself. This suggests I need to repeat `Plane.20009` across the bases. The original prompt\'s reference to `FactoryPlaygroundCanvas` is where my attention will focus.\n\n\n**Confirming Perimeter Placement**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing the code\'s perimeter placements. It confirms the \"edge-to-edge\" barricade wall intent. Lines 222-224 confirm the placement of the \'barricade\' asset. Lines 183-208 confirm that there is indeed an \"edge-to-edge\" barrier, and shows an example of repetitive fence placement coordinates that is helpful to reference.\n\n\n**Calculating Fence Dimensions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise dimensions of a single `concrete_fence` unit. I\'ve found multiple placements in the code, but I need to calculate the actual length to determine the exact spacing needed for the \"edge-to-edge\" barricade walls and understand the gaps in perimeter walls. This is crucial for properly repeating the fence along the bases.\n\n\n"
