  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Calculating Gate Post Positions**\n\nI\'ve determined that `lx = 18.8` corresponds to setting the gate post group\'s position to (18.8, 0, -3.1). The opposite catch post is 6.2 units away along the Z-axis, placing it at `lz = +3.1`. The world coordinates are established with `hqX = -46.5` and `hqZ = 39.0`.\n\n\n**Refining Gate Coordinates**\n\nI\'ve refined the gate\'s world coordinates: its x-position is approximately -27.5. The Z-coordinates span from 35.9 to 42.1, indicating a width of roughly 6.2 meters. The North wall extends from the NE corner bastion down to z = 35.9, while the South wall runs from the gate at z = 42.1 to the SE corner. I\'m now integrating the concrete fence model, replacing barricade placements within the team base quadrants.\n\n\n**Analyzing Fence Placement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on precise placement of the `concrete_fence` model around the base. My goal is edge-to-edge construction, fully encompassing the bases without gaps, and preserving the original submesh structure of the fence model. I need to be sure the fence\'s placement fully encloses the base, including the gate area. I\'m also double-checking if there are any other instances of `concrete-fence-1a.glb` and barricades within `FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx`. It looks like barricades are used as editor tools, and in the model, but I need to make sure this is accurate. I see the existing barricade is at x=-26.2, z=34.8.\n\n\n**Confirming Fence Replacement Scope**\n\nI\'ve determined I need to replace *all* barricades around the Blue and Red bases with the concrete fence model, keeping the original sub-mesh structure. The prompt clearly specifies this, and I\'m now certain this excludes the crane dock barricades. I\'m focusing solely on replacing the barricades around the bases with the concrete fence model now, and I\'m keeping track of which barricades need to be replaced.\n\n\n"
