    thinking: "**Reviewing Asset Loading**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving back into `spawnRealLyoPropFromGlb`. I\'m double-checking it, alongside `concrete-fence-1a.glb`, to see if there\'s any sub-mesh modification or stripping happening. I need to make sure this isn\'t affecting the assets. I\'ve re-opened `spawnRealLyoPropFromGlb` in `src` to conduct a thorough review.\n\n\n**Analyzing Mesh Traversal**\n\nI\'ve just focused on the traversal function within `lyoAssetsAndShaders.ts`. I\'m closely examining how meshes are handled, specifically the conditional logic to differentiate `dumpTruck` assets. I\'m keen to understand the implications of `buildDumpTruckGeometryWithoutPipes` and how it might be affecting asset integrity. My review extends to the material upgrades and shadow casting, assessing potential performance implications as well.\n\n\n**Confirming Asset Preservation**\n\nI\'ve just had a breakthrough! Analyzing `orientedRoot` clarifies that the sub-mesh structure is meticulously preserved during cloning and positioning. Each mesh is cloned, retaining its exact transform, material, and stroke outline. This confirms the original asset\'s integrity. Further investigation into fence placement within `FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx` is underway to validate this within the broader context.\n\n\n**Constructing Perimeter Defenses**\n\nI\'ve just finished the military base master plan, focusing on perimeter defenses within the specified coordinates. I\'m placing concrete fences along the north, south, and west perimeter walls. I\'m carefully determining the positions and orientations to ensure proper coverage and defense capabilities.\n\n\n**Implementing Infrastructure Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the detailed components, like utility pipes and heavy vehicle exhausts, into the master plan. Specifically, I\'m focusing on their precise placement on the Central Command HQ and the Heavy Vehicle Hangar, ensuring they align correctly with the buildings. I\'ve also integrated fuel storage depot assets, like tanks and explosive barrels, into the correct coordinates.\n\n\n**Updating Asset Placement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the prop placements for the Ack\'s Yard area within the FactoryPlaygroundCanvas.tsx file. I\'m updating the file content, replacing the existing lines (183-228) with the defined prop placement. This includes new assets like a wheelbarrow, hydrant, barricades, and lampposts.\n\n\n**Defining Fence Parameters**\n\nI\'m now precisely defining concrete fence placement. I\'m focusing on the north, south, and west perimeter walls, meticulously setting coordinates and orientations. The east perimeter wall is being configured with a main security gate. I\'ve been considering spacing for proper coverage and integrating this within the existing coordinate system.\n\n\n**Integrating Prop Placement**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided coordinates into the master plan for fence and prop placement. I\'m focusing on concrete fences, utility pipe clusters, heavy vehicle exhausts, fuel storage depots, and yard props like wheelbarrows and hydrants. Specifically, I\'m integrating these placements into my overall system for precise location definition and asset integration, as they relate to my master plan.\n\n\n"
